{
    "background_story": "Shepard was a decorated war veteran who had seen his fair share of battles. After leaving the military, he settled in the city of Taegu, South Korea, where he had been stationed during his service. The city held a special place in his heart, and he felt a deep connection to its people and culture. Shepard spent his days volunteering at a local orphanage, teaching the children English and sharing stories of his adventures. He became a beloved figure in the community, known for his kind heart and generosity. As he explored the city, Shepard discovered the rich history and traditions of Taegu, and he made it his mission to learn as much as he could. He became particularly fond of the city's famous night markets, where he would often take the children on special outings. Shepard's love for Taegu and its people had brought him a sense of purpose and belonging he never thought he'd find again.",
